'''Jimmon Arbmab''', designation '''HC-4120''', was a [[human]]<ref name="Geektionary French" /> [[Gender|male]] [[Imperial combat assault tank commander]] part of the [[Imperial Hammers Elite Armor Unit]].<ref name="UVG" /> Arbmab served as a [[First Sergeant]] and commanded a [[TX-225 GAVw "Occupier" combat assault tank]] through the streets of [[Jedha City]] when the [[tank]] was ambushed by [[Saw Gerrera]]'s [[Partisans]]. In the ensuing [[Battle on Jedha|battle]], Arbmab was [[Death|killed]] by a blast from [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor's]] [[Cassian Andor's blaster|A280-CFE]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Biography==
[[File:Armored_Patrol_SWR-RotE.png|thumb|left|250px|Arbmab commanding a combat tank on Jedha.]]
Jimmon Arbmab was a [[human]]<ref name="Geektionary French" /> [[Gender|male]] who served the [[Galactic Empire]] as an [[Imperial combat assault tank commander]] with the designation HC-4120 in the [[Imperial Hammers Elite Armor Unit]]. Arbmab was promoted to the position of [[First Sergeant]] and deployed along with his unit to the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] [[moon]] of [[Jedha]].<ref name="UVG" />

While stationed on the [[desert]] moon, he and his [[TX-225 GAVw "Occupier" combat assault tank|tank]] crew were assigned to the transport security of [[kyber crystal]]s being exported from moon's main hub, [[Jedha City]]. Shortly before the Empire evacuated all troops from the moon, Arbmab and his crew were part of a kyber transport detail that consisted of his tank and a [[squad]] of [[stormtrooper]]s. The tank and its escort were subsequently ambushed by [[partisans]] loyal to the rebel leader [[Saw Gerrera]]. Many members of the escort were killed, including Arbmab, when [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], a [[spy]] on a mission from the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], shot and [[Death|killed]] the tank commander from his position on the tank.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Equipment==
Arbmab wore the standard [[Color|white]] [[plastoid]] [[Stormtrooper armor|armor]] of an Imperial tank commander, including the gray markings that denoted his rank.<ref name="UVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Jimmon Arbmab was portrayed uncredited<ref name="Rogue One" /> by [[Louis Samms]]<ref name="Facebook">{{Facebook|username=Skywalkersignings-uk-101887251657960|url=watch/?v=310806670463891|name=Skywalkersignings uk|date=2021-04-04|archiveurl=https://archive.md/Nf0Xv}}</ref> in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology]] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''<ref name="Rogue One" /> and was first identified in the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and released alongside the film.<ref name="UVG" /> The character of Arbmab originated in the [[1989]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] short story ''[[The Assault on Protazk]]'', which was published in the role-playing reference book the ''[[Imperial Sourcebook]]'', which was written by [[Greg Gorden]] for the ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]''.<ref name="Imperial Sourcebook">{{WEGCite|story=The Assault on Protazk|book=Imperial Sourcebook}}</ref>

